  "residuals": [
    "Recovery defaults remain enabled in common and recovery fstab selection unresolved; the first SD media still must exclude it through verified platform build and packaging rules.",
    "drmserver (Android media DRM), drmservice policy definitions and /dev/rknand_sys_storage generic ownership remain unchanged; removing the separate automatic vendor drmservice is not a statement that all DRM is disabled or raw storage inaccessible.",
    "OP-TEE import removed from changed board init only; other inherited init imports/packages may reintroduce it.",
    "Vendor BT blobs remain in upstream sources but their six copy entries are omitted. Final image Bluetooth absence cannot be asserted until full product and generated file inventory are inspected.",
    "Platform core_minimal and other unresolved inheritance may supply Bluetooth packages, feature XML, init services or update/install/recovery routes. No BT feature XML copy was found in the examined common TV permissions or wifi_bt_common; none was fabricated or removed by guess.",
    "Wi-Fi selection and source settings remain Broadcom/ap6xxx defaults as before; these are not an identification of the actual unit and no wireless compatibility is implied.",
    "The generic kernel reference still has Bluetooth/NAND enabled; this source patchset does not create a hardware-safe SD kernel profile.",
    "No SELinux policy was compiled and no runtime behavior was validated; source-level omission and replay only.",
    "Disabled dhcpcd_bt-pan and iprenew_bt-pan services remain in init.rockchip.rc, as do unrelated net_bt_stack group references. Enumerated service/package/grant exclusions are not removal of every Bluetooth-related string or proof of a Bluetooth-free generated product."
  ],
